Term]\nid: MONDO:0020735\nname: ACTH-independent macronodular adrenal hyperplasia 1\ndef: \"Any Cushing syndrome due to macronodular adrenal hyperplasia in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the GNAS1 gene.\" [OMIM:219080]\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0111623\"}\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0025230\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: nord_rare {source=\"MONDO:NORD\"}\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:219080\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"ACTH-independent macronodular adrenal hyperplasia\" BROAD []\nsynonym: \"ACTH-independent macronodular adrenal hyperplasia 1\" EXACT [DOID:0111623, OMIM:219080]\nsynonym: \"ACTH-independent macronodular adrenal hyperplasia, Somatic mutation\" EXACT []\nsynonym: \"ACTH-independent macronodular adrenocortical hyperplasia\" EXACT [GARD:0010824, MESH:C565662, OMIM:219080]\nsynonym: \"adrenocorticotropic hormone-independent macronodular adrenal hyperplasia\" EXACT [GARD:0010824, MESH:C565662, OMIM:219080]\nsynonym: \"AIMAH1\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [DOID:0111623, MESH:C565662, OMIM:219080]\nsynonym: \"corticotropin-independent macronodular adrenal hyperplasia\" EXACT [GARD:0010824, MESH:C565662, OMIM:219080]\nsynonym: \"Cushing syndrome, adrenal, due to AIMAH\" EXACT [MESH:C565662, OMIM:219080]\nxref: DOID:0111623 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: GARD:0025230 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:347456 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: OMIM:219080 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"Orphanet:189427\", source=\"GARD:0010824\", source=\"Orphanet:189427/e\"}\nxref: UMLS:C1857451 {source=\"MEDGEN:347456\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0009049 {source=\"DOID:0111623\", source=\"MONDO:prototype\"} ! Cushing syndrome due to macronodular adrenal hyperplasia\nintersection_of: MONDO:0009049 ! Cushing syndrome due to macronodular adrenal hyperplasia\nintersection_of: RO:0004004 http://identifiers.org/hgnc/4392 ! has material basis in somatic mutation in GNAS\nrelationship: RO:0004004 http://identifiers.org/hgnc/4392 {source=\"OMIM:219080\"} ! has material basis in somatic mutation in GNAS\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/acth_independent_macronodular_adrenal_hyperplasia_1\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/4521\" xsd:anyURI\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/6475\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0100168\nname: desmoid tumor caused by somatic mutation\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0111349\"}\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0026071\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: DOID:0111349 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: GARD:0026071 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:436434 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C2675440 {source=\"MEDGEN:436434\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0007608 {source=\"OMIM:135290\"} ! desmoid tumor\nrelationship: excluded_from_qc_check http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/sparql/qc/general/qc-single-child.sparql\nrelationship: RO:0004004 http://identifiers.org/hgnc/583 {source=\"OMIM:135290\"} ! has material basis in somatic mutation in APC\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/2808#issuecomment-797765939\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1030005\nname: mosaic SMO syndrome\ndef: \"A somatic mosaic condition caused by a postzygotic mutation (c.1234 C>T p.Leu412Phe) in the SMO gene. Two overlapping clinical syndromes associated with this variant in SMO have been reported; Curry-Jones Syndrome (MIM:601707) and Happle-Tinschert Syndrome. The syndrome is characterized by cutaneous and skeletal manifestations such as linear hypo‐ or hyperpigmented lesions, basaloid follicular hamartomas, palmoplantar pitting, atrophoderma, hypertrichosis, polydactyly or syndactyly, rib anomalies (rudimentary ribs), and limb‐length anomalies. Craniofacial and dental abnormalities such as dysmorphic facies, macrocephaly, craniosynostosis, jaw tumors (ameloblastoma) have also been reported. Additional abnormalities impacting the gastrointestinal, cerebral, ophthalmic, and gonadal organs should also be considered. Some of these features include anal anomaly, colonic adenocarcinoma, severe constipation, myelofibrosis and smooth muscle hamartomas, malrotation, medulloblastoma, cerebral malformations, developmental delay, cataract, microphthalmia, coloboma, glaucoma, and cryptorchidism.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40059/, PMID:27236920, PMID:30497210, PMID:31120550, PMID:32413283, PMID:7606318]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0027231\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: GARD:0027231 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0015160 {source=\"PMID:31120550\"} ! multiple congenital anomalies/dysmorphic syndrome-variable intellectual disability syndrome\nrelationship: RO:0004004 http://identifiers.org/hgnc/11119 {source=\"PMID:31120550\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40059/\"} ! has material basis in somatic mutation in SMO\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3458-4839\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7768\" xsd:anyURI\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
